The [[Celadon Gym]] specializes in {{type|Grass}} Pokémon. Grass-type moves are super effective against {{t|Ground}}-, {{t|Rock}}-, and {{type|Water}} Pokémon, while Grass-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Bug}}-, {{t|Fire}}-, {{t|Flying}}-, {{t|Ice}}-, and {{type|Poison}} moves.

The Gym is designed as a greenhouse, with many flower arrangements on display. Use {{m|Cut}} to clear a path and pass under the first archway. Turn left, pass by Twins Jo & Zoe, then move in a clockwise "C" direction. Loop around the flowerbed in the middle of the Gym to pass under the archway in the southeast corner, then go north. Continue on past Picnicker Tanya, then turn west. Pass by Beauty Julia and walk under the middle and western archways. Use Cut a second and third time to remove two more small trees to reach the [[Gym Leader]].

[[Erika]] leads with her {{p|Jumpluff}}. Both {{m|Leech Seed}} and {{m|Giga Drain}} steal the target's {{stat|HP}}, and {{m|Sunny Day}} triggers its {{a|Chlorophyll}} Ability to boost its already-high {{stat|Speed}}. As a {{2t|Grass|Flying}} Pokémon, it takes massive damage from {{type|Ice}} attacks. Her {{p|Tangela}} can further harass its target with {{m|Sleep Powder}}, and {{m|Ancient Power|AncientPower}} lets it fight back against the {{t|Grass}} type's common counters: {{t|Fire}}, Ice, {{t|Bug}}, and {{t|Flying}} Pokémon. {{p|Victreebel}}'s {{m|Leaf Storm}} is powerful, but cuts its {{stat|Special Attack}} with every use. As plants rely on the sun for nutrients, Erika's remaining two Pokémon rely on {{m|Sunny Day}} to prepare their combination moves. {{p|Victreebel}} regains more HP than normal under [[harsh sunlight]] with {{m|Synthesis}}, and {{p|Bellossom}} does the same. Under these conditions, Bellossom can launch its strongest move, {{m|SolarBeam}}, without first taking a turn to charge it.

